      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Multiplying a matrix by a scalar is also straightforward. If $ M = aN $, where $ a $ is a scalar, then $ M_{ij} = aN_{ij} $. Each element of $ N $ is simply multiplied by the scalar. For example,",
      "source_page": 200,
      "printed_page": 180,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p200:b3"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        135.0,
        176.0,
        1094.0,
        273.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_chapter8_formula018]]",
      "source_page": 200,
      "printed_page": 180,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p200:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
